IOAudioFamily for Minkar
========================

Our own implementation (BSD-2-Clause) of the audio driver family:
IOAudioDevice, IOAudioEngine, IOAudioStream, IOAudioControl,
IOAudioLevelControl, IOAudioToggleControl and the engine's user client.
It follows the family's public API so that drivers written for it build
here; it is not binary compatible with the reference platform's kext and
contains none of its code (that code is published under the Apple Public
Source License 1.1, which Minkar does not take in).

The bundle identifier is com.apple.iokit.IOAudioFamily, the name drivers
list in OSBundleLibraries.

How it works:

* A driver's IOAudioDevice sets its hardware up in initHardware() and
  activates an IOAudioEngine for each sample buffer the hardware runs.
* The engine's streams hold the formats the hardware takes, the one in use
  and the sample buffer (the hardware's own DMA buffer).
* The driver stamps every wrap of the buffer (takeTimeStamp): the loop
  count and its time are in a status page clients map, written under a
  sequence number so a reader never mixes two wraps.
* There is no mixing or sample conversion in the kernel: Minkar's audio
  service maps the buffers (IOAudioEngineUserClient) and writes and reads
  the device's own format in place, ahead of the hardware. clipOutputSamples
  and convertInputSamples answer kIOReturnUnsupported.
* Controls (volume, mute) call the driver's value change handler; a client
  sets them through the registry (IOAudioControlValue).

Not implemented yet: IOAudioPort, IOAudioSelectorControl, the family's
power management, the classic mix buffers and their user client protocol,
input streams' erase head.
